isdom"],[11.988,0.1,"The"],[12.1,0.375,"wise"],[12.488,0.412,"grieve"],[12.912,0.412,"neither"],[13.338,0.163,"for"],[13.512,0.113,"the"],[13.637,0.425,"living"],[14.075,0.35,"nor"],[14.438,0.163,"for"],[14.613,0.1,"the"],[14.725,0.412,"dead"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"The Self that never dies","visual":["There was never a time when we did not exist","Weapons do not cut it, fire does not burn it","It is eternal, unchanging, all-pervading"],"L":["L1"],"say":"Krishna begins with the deepest truth of all. There was never a time when Arjuna, Krishna, or these kings did not exist, and there never will be. Weapons cannot cut the Spirit, fire cannot burn it, water cannot wet it, and wind cannot dry it. What Arjuna fears to destroy cannot be destroyed.","start":77.064,"at":77.64,"end":98.664,"words":[[0.087,0.45,"Krishna"],[0.55,0.55,"begins"],[1.113,0.2,"with"],[1.325,0.125,"the"],[1.462,0.425,"deepest"],[1.9,0.312,"truth"],[2.225,0.1,"of"],[2.337,0.362,"all"],[3.087,0.087,"There"],[3.188,0.125,"was"],[3.325,0.3,"never"],[3.638,0.05,"a"],[3.7,0.375,"time"],[4.088,0.163,"when"],[4.263,0.613,"Arjuna"],[4.888,0.613,"Krishna"],[5.737,0.188,"or"],[5.938,0.212,"these"],[6.162,0.338,"kings"],[6.513,0.138,"did"],[6.662,0.212,"not"],[6.888,0.6,"exist"],[7.662,0.175,"and"],[7.85,0.125,"there"],[7.987,0.325,"never"],[8.325,0.188,"will"],[8.525,0.3,"be"],[9.225,0.412,"Weapons"],[9.65,0.338,"cannot"],[10.0,0.212,"cut"],[10.225,0.075,"the"],[10.312,0.487,"Spirit"],[11.4,0.425,"fire"],[11.838,0.35,"cannot"],[12.2,0.237,"burn"],[12.45,0.175,"it"],[13.262,0.375,"water"],[13.65,0.362,"cannot"],[14.025,0.175,"wet"],[14.213,0.175,"it"],[14.938,0.138,"and"],[15.088,0.4,"wind"],[15.5,0.338,"cannot"],[15.85,0.25,"dry"],[16.113,0.2,"it"],[16.688,0.212,"What"],[16.925,0.475,"Arjuna"],[17.413,0.45,"fears"],[17.875,0.125,"to"],[18.012,0.562,"destroy"],[18.587,0.4,"cannot"],[19.0,0.113,"be"],[19.125,0.662,"destroyed"]]},{"layout":"verse","headline":"","visual":[],"L":["L4"],"ref":"2.22","verse":"Just as a person puts on new garments after discarding the old ones; similarly, the living entity acquires new bodies after casting away the old bodies.","key":true,"vs":[14,40],"say":"Then comes one of the most loved images in the whole Gita. Verse twenty-two. Just as a person puts on new garments after discarding the old ones; similarly, the living entity acquires new bodies after casting away the old bodies.","start":98.664,"at":99.24,"end":115.392,"words":[[0.087,0.225,"Then"],[0.325,0.3,"comes"],[0.637,0.175,"one"],[0.825,0.062,"of"],[0.9,0.075,"the"],[0.988,0.338,"most"],[1.337,0.338,"loved"],[1.688,0.562,"images"],[2.263,0.163,"in"],[2.438,0.05,"the"],[2.5,0.263,"whole"],[2.775,0.45,"Gita"],[3.612,0.388,"Verse"],[4.013,0.7,"twenty-two"],[5.112,0.3,"Just"],[5.425,0.1,"as"],[5.537,0.075,"a"],[5.625,0.388,"person"],[6.025,0.263,"puts"],[6.3,0.138,"on"],[6.45,0.188,"new"],[6.65,0.512,"garments"],[7.188,0.287,"after"],[7.487,0.512,"discarding"],[8.012,0.062,"the"],[8.088,0.25,"old"],[8.35,0.388,"ones"],[9.412,0.738,"similarly"],[10.338,0.138,"the"],[10.488,0.338,"living"],[10.838,0.425,"entity"],[11.275,0.5,"acquires"],[11.787,0.175,"new"],[11.975,0.475,"bodies"],[12.463,0.287,"after"],[12.762,0.438,"casting"],[13.213,0.287,"away"],[13.512,0.075,"the"],[13.6,0.225,"old"],[13.838,0.512,"bodies"]]},{"layout":"story","headline":"The duty of a warrior","visual":["A just war is a duty, not a crime","Running away would bring dishonour","Treat victory and defeat alike"],"L":["L3"],"say":"Krishna then speaks to Arjuna as a warrior. For one whose duty is to protect, there is nothing higher than a fight for what is right. To walk away now would not be peace. It would be a failure of duty, and the world would remember it as fear. So Krishna asks him to treat pleasure and pain, gain and loss, victory and defeat alike, and simply do what is right.","start":115.392,"at":115.968,"end":140.616,"words":[[0.087,0.463,"Krishna"],[0.562,0.263,"then"],[0.838,0.45,"speaks"],[1.3,0.11